From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wayland-egl: create the wl_egl_window at least 1x1

QWaylandGLContext::makeCurrent() creates the EGL surface from the window's
buffer size. A QML window that has not been sized yet, and has not been
configured by the compositor, is 0x0 at its first render. libwayland-egl's
wl_egl_window_create() returns NULL when either dimension is 0 (and accepts
1x1), so no EGL surface is created and the context cannot be made current:

  QWARNING: Could not create wl_egl_window with size 0x0
  QWARNING: QWaylandGLContext::makeCurrent: eglError: 0x3009
  QWARNING: QRhiGles2: Failed to make context current. Expect bad things to happen.
  QWARNING: Failed to create RHI (backend 2)
  QFATAL: Failed to initialize graphics backend for OpenGL.

The application aborts before it has shown anything. On LuneOS this is what
happens to the Settings pages (Appearance, Device Info, ...) on a Halium device.

Clamp the size to at least 1x1 in createSurface() and updateSurfaceSize(). The
real size is applied by wl_egl_window_resize() as soon as the compositor has
configured the window. QWaylandGLContext already creates its dummy window
with 1x1 for the same reason.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@
     return m_bufferSize;
 }
 
-void QWaylandEglWindow::updateSurfaceSize(const QSize &initialSize)
+void QWaylandEglWindow::updateSurfaceSize(const QSize &requestedSize)
 {
     // potentially called from a render thread
     // eglSurfaceLock should be locked before calling this method
@@ -76,6 +76,9 @@
     if (!m_waylandEglWindow)
         return;
 
+    // wl_egl_windows must have both width and height > 0
+    const QSize initialSize(qMax(requestedSize.width(), 1), qMax(requestedSize.height(), 1));
+
     int current_width = 0;
     int current_height = 0;
     static bool disableResizeCheck = qgetenv("QT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_RESIZECHECK").toInt();
@@ -91,11 +94,15 @@
     }
 }
 
-void QWaylandEglWindow::createSurface(const QSize &initialSize)
+void QWaylandEglWindow::createSurface(const QSize &requestedSize)
 {
     // potentially called from a render thread
     // eglSurfaceLock should be locked before calling this method
 
+    // wl_egl_window_create() returns NULL if either dimension is 0, and the window
+    // is 0x0 until the compositor has configured it, so make sure the size is at least 1
+    const QSize initialSize(qMax(requestedSize.width(), 1), qMax(requestedSize.height(), 1));
+
     QReadLocker locker(&mSurfaceLock);
     if (mSurface) {
         wl_egl_window *eglWindow = wl_egl_window_create(mSurface->object(), initialSize.width(), initialSize.height());
